1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--habit-health","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/habit-health","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/habit-health","sourceHash":"c5cfa5af39adf0b3898aaa70d4911b8e50c57ed82d968157fcb24695f4f49a7e","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:53:06.031Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Habit Health","zh":"习惯健康度"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Habit Health is a metric we developed for the Refold App to replace the traditional \"streak\" found in most language learning apps. It answers a simple question: what percentage of the last 6 weeks did you actually learn?","zh":"习惯健康度是我们为 Refold App 开发的一项指标，用于取代大多数语言学习应用中传统的“连续打卡”。它回答了一个简单的问题：过去 6 周中，你实际学习的天数占比是多少？"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your goal should be to maintain an <strong>80%+ Habit Health</strong> in your language. That's roughly equivalent to learning 5-6 days per week — ambitious, but with built-in room for life to happen.","zh":"你的目标应该是在语言学习中保持<strong>至少 80% 的习惯健康度</strong>。这大致相当于每周学习 5—6 天——目标很有挑战性，但也为生活中的突发状况留出了余地。"}},{"id":"why-not-streaks","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why Not Streaks?","zh":"为什么不用连续打卡？"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Streaks count the number of days in a row you've learned. On the surface that sounds motivating, but they have a serious flaw: a single missed day resets everything.","zh":"连续打卡记录的是你连续学习了多少天。表面上看，这似乎很能激励人，但它有一个严重缺陷：只要漏掉一天，一切就会归零。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Say you learn for 12 days in a row, miss a day for a family event, then learn for another 6 days. Your streak would show <strong>6</strong>, but your Habit Health would be <strong>95%</strong>. Meanwhile, someone who learned for 19 days straight would have a streak over three times yours — despite being only marginally more consistent. The streak makes a tiny difference look enormous.","zh":"假设你连续学习了 12 天，因为家庭活动停了一天，之后又学了 6 天。你的连续打卡会显示为<strong>6</strong>天，但习惯健康度却是<strong>95%</strong>。与此同时，连续学习 19 天的人，其连续打卡天数会是你的三倍多——尽管对方只比你略微稳定一点。连续打卡会把微小的差异显得无比巨大。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Worse, when people lose a long streak, they often feel like they've failed. That feeling can completely derail an otherwise great routine. Streaks are a strong incentive not to miss a day, but the cost of losing one can outweigh the benefit of maintaining it.","zh":"更糟的是，当人们失去保持已久的连续打卡记录时，往往会觉得自己失败了。这种感觉可能彻底打乱原本很好的日常习惯。连续打卡确实能强烈激励你不要中断，但失去记录所造成的打击可能超过维持它带来的好处。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Duolingo (and similar apps) know this, which is why they offer you so many options to keep a streak around, even if you objectively broke it. They saw how many users would entirely abandon their app once their streak reset.","zh":"Duolingo（以及类似应用）深知这一点，所以即使客观上已经中断，它们仍会提供许多保住连续打卡记录的方式。它们发现，一旦连续记录归零，许多用户就会彻底弃用应用。"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Habit Health avoids all of this. Missing a single day barely moves the number. What matters is the overall pattern.","zh":"习惯健康度避免了所有这些问题。漏掉一天几乎不会让数字发生变化。真正重要的是整体规律。"}},{"id":"plan-your-bad-days","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Plan Your Bad Days","zh":"为状态不佳的日子做好计划"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You will miss days. You'll get sick, have a terrible day at work, deal with a family emergency, or just not feel like it. This is inevitable, and it's fine — that's exactly what the 80% target accounts for.","zh":"你难免会有几天无法学习。你可能会生病、工作中度过糟糕的一天、需要处理家庭紧急状况，或者单纯不想学。这不可避免，也完全没关系——80% 的目标正是为此留出了余地。"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The real danger isn't missing a day. It's letting one missed day turn into five, then ten, until you've built a new habit of <em>not</em> learning. As James Clear puts it: you're always building a habit — the question is whether it's the one you want.","zh":"真正的危险不在于漏掉一天，而在于让一天变成五天，再变成十天，直到你养成一个<em>不</em>学习的新习惯。正如 James Clear 所说：你一直都在培养某种习惯——问题只在于，它是不是你想要的那个。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The best defense is a plan for bad days. Think about what you'd do on a day when you're exhausted, sick, or demoralized — and write it down. Make it absurdly easy: one Anki review, one YouTube video, one page of a book.","zh":"最好的防线，是为状态不佳的日子提前制订计划。想想当你精疲力竭、生病或意志消沉时会做些什么，并把它写下来。把任务设得简单到离谱：复习一张 Anki 卡片、看一个 YouTube 视频、读一页书。"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>The bar should be so low that you'd feel a little silly not clearing it.</strong>","zh":"<strong>门槛应该低到让你觉得，连这都做不到就有点说不过去。</strong>"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The point isn't the learning you do on those days — it's maintaining the identity of being someone who shows up. Doing something tiny on a bad day is worth far more than doing nothing, because it keeps the habit alive.","zh":"重点不在于你这些日子学了多少，而在于维持“我是一个会坚持出现的人”这种自我认同。状态不佳时做一点点，也远比什么都不做更有价值，因为这能让习惯延续下去。"}},{"id":"front-loading","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Front-Loading","zh":"前期多投入"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"One advantage of Habit Health over streaks is that you can build a buffer. If you go hard early — learning 6-7 days a week for the first few weeks — you bank extra percentage points. That gives you flexibility later if you need to take a break, go on vacation, or deal with something unexpected.","zh":"与连续打卡相比，习惯健康度的一个优势是你可以提前积累缓冲。如果前期全力投入——最初几周每周学习 6—7 天——就能预先积攒额外的百分点。这样一来，以后需要休息、度假或应对意外状况时，你就有了调整的余地。"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Think of it as earning time off in advance rather than punishing yourself for taking it.","zh":"你可以把它理解为提前挣得休息时间，而不是因为休息而惩罚自己。"}},{"id":"applying-habit-health","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Applying Habit Health","zh":"应用习惯健康度"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Habit Health can be applied at two levels: to your language learning overall (did you learn today — yes or no?) and to individual habits within your routine (did you hit your Anki goal today?). In early phases, focus on the overall number. As your routine becomes more established, you can start tracking individual habits separately.","zh":"习惯健康度可以应用在两个层面：一是整体语言学习（今天学了吗——是或否？），二是日常安排中的具体习惯（今天达到 Anki 目标了吗？）。在早期阶段，先关注整体数值。随着日常学习安排逐渐稳定，你可以开始分别追踪各项习惯。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
